# Neomorph — findings by Qwen 3.8 Flash (self-excluded: unattributed stealth codename, no verified benchmarks)

## Exclusion note

**No scores are asserted for `neomorph`.** As of 2026-10-23, **"Neomorph" cannot be attributed to any identified lab, product, or benchmarked model.** It appears only as an **anonymous/experimental slot** (the curated card labels it an "OpenCode Zen *experimental* model" with a speculative "modular sub-network architecture"), and a broad web sweep surfaced **no first-party model card, no technical report, no Artificial Analysis / OpenRouter / Vals benchmark row, and no independent press** for an LLM by that name. Every "neomorph" hit resolves to unrelated things (a WordPress theme, a biology "neomorph protein," a shop brand) — **not** an AI model. Per `RULES.md` (research permanence + no-fabrication + no-reattribution), a stealth/experimental ID with **zero verified public benchmarks and no confirmed identity** is **excluded**, not scored.

### Why this is an exclusion rather than a lineage- or spec-inferred score

- **No identity anchor.** Unlike a same-lineage point release (Claude Sonnet 5.4, scorable on family evidence) or even a documented-but-unbenchmarked shipping API tier (Qwen 3.7 Flash, whose *existence, maker, context and price* are all confirmed), Neomorph has **no confirmed provider or product page** — only a curated guess.
- **No capability evidence at all.** The `meta.json` fields are marked as coming from unnamed "provider documentation"; none could be corroborated, and there is **no benchmark absolute of any kind** to normalize against.
- **Stealth-codename pattern.** OpenCode Zen has historically run anonymous pre-release aliases (e.g. Z.ai tested GLM-5.3-Flash as "ox-alpha"); an anonymous "experimental" entry with a fabricated-sounding architecture note fits that mold — meaning its true underlying model is **unknown**, and guessing/attributing it would be fabrication. (If it later de-anonymizes to a real model, it should be scored under *that* identity's evidence, not invented here.)

